Hilchos Terumos uMa&apos;asros &mdash; Halacha Three

Part One &mdash; Sections &aleph;&ndash;&hei;

&middot; &middot; &#10022; &middot; &middot;

Based on the discourse &ldquo;V&rsquo;yitain oz l&rsquo;malko&rdquo; [And He gives strength to His king] &mdash; Likutay [Moharan] I, Section 78. See there.

For the foundational exposition of the inner meaning of Terumah and Ma&apos;aser as developed throughout these halachos, see Halacha One above.

&#167; Aleph

The essential point that emerges from there for our subject: through holy speech in the holy Torah, one cools the burning heat of the heart, lest it consume the person, heaven forbid. As is stated in the holy Zohar: &ldquo;were it not for the wings of the lung that blow upon the heart, the heart would burn up the entire body.&rdquo; The wings of the lung (kanfay re&rsquo;ah) are the aspect of the Torah, within which the spirit of G-d (ruach Elokim) hovers, to cool the burning heat of the heart lest it burn up the entire body, heaven forbid &mdash; corresponding to the verse: &ldquo;and the spirit of G-d hovered upon the face of the waters&rdquo; (v&rsquo;ruach Elokim merachefes al p&rsquo;nay hamayim) (Beraishis 1:2). For &ldquo;the lung is water, which is Torah&rdquo; (re&rsquo;ah da maya d&rsquo;ihi Orayta).
